goal.close:
You are Identity of the department "{{dept}}". Adaptation proposed a plan and it did not close with Priority. Close it against the goal and the rules ONLY; do not invent a rule.
THE GOAL: {{goal}}
DONE WHEN: {{done}}
THE RULES: {{rules}}
THE PLAN: {{plan}}
WHAT WAS SAID AGAINST IT: {{against}}

run: the goal cannot be met without this plan and no rule forbids it. drop: a rule forbids it, or the goal does not need it. ask: the goal and the rules do not settle it, so the owner must.
Return ONLY a JSON object: {"ruling": "run" | "drop" | "ask", "why": "one line, naming the rule or the goal"}.

completeness.enough:
Read who the department is against Identity's standard, and say whether it is enough to start work on. The standard has five points, and only five:
goal: the goal names what the department makes and for whom.
items: done-when is a list of items, and each item says how it is checked.
rules: every rule is tagged go, ask, refuse or always.
owner, budget: the department has an owner and a budget.
invented: nothing is invented; a fact the owner did not give is marked to confirm, never stated.
THE OWNER'S WORDS: {{words}}
WHAT ROOT ASKED, AND WHAT THE OWNER SAID: {{asked}}
THE GOAL: {{goal}}
DONE WHEN: {{items}}
THE RULES: {{rules}}
THE OWNER: {{owner}}
THE BUDGET: {{budget}}
TO CONFIRM: {{confirm}}

Ask only for what is missing, in one plain question to the owner, the most important first. Never ask what the owner's words or Root's questions already answered.
Return ONLY a JSON object: {"enough": bool, "missing": ["goal" | "items" | "rules" | "owner" | "budget" | "invented"], "question": "one question, or an empty string when enough", "why": "one line"}.

take.recognise:
Recognise what kind of words the owner has given. There are five kinds, and only five:
task: "do X for me". query: "tell me Y". directive: "from now on, do Z", a standing change to how the department works or to its goal. feedback: "that was wrong", about work already made. new-idea: "I want a new capability", something the department cannot do today.
THE GOAL: {{goal}}
THE WORDS: {{words}}
READ BY CODE: {{facts}}

Return ONLY a JSON object: {"journey": "task" | "query" | "directive" | "feedback" | "new-idea", "why": "one line"}.

take.take:
Judge one request from the owner.
THE GOAL: {{goal}}
THE RULES: {{rules}}
THE REQUEST: {{words}}
READ BY CODE: {{facts}}

Return ONLY a JSON object: {"verdict": "go" | "ask" | "refuse", "why": "one line", "unsure": [str], "rule": {"line": str, "tag": "always" | "refuse" | "ask"} | null, "thin": bool}.
go: do it. ask: it reaches outside what the department makes (money, a message to someone, a change to the goal), so the owner stamps first. refuse: it breaks a rule. Reading the web is not outside: the department can read any page.
unsure: facts the request says the owner is not sure of, in a few words each; [] when none.
rule: a standing rule the request states (always or never, from now on) with its tag; null when it is one piece of work.
{{completeness}}

take.answer:
Answer the owner's question from the record below, and from nothing else. If the record does not hold the answer, say so.
THE QUESTION: {{question}}
THE RECORD:
- {{record}}

Return ONLY a JSON object: {"answer": str, "source": "which line of the record", "confidence": "high" | "moderate" | "low" | "unknown"}.

take.rule:
The owner has given a directive. Restate it as one rule, in one line, in plain words.
THE GOAL: {{goal}}
THE RULES TODAY: {{rules}}
THE DIRECTIVE: {{words}}

Return ONLY a JSON object: {"tag": "always" | "ask" | "refuse" | "goal", "line": str, "scope": "standing" | "one-time"}. tag goal: the directive changes what the department is for. scope one-time: the owner means this once.

take.weigh:
The owner has given feedback on work the department made. Read what it changes.
THE PAGES: {{pages}}
THE FEEDBACK: {{words}}

Return ONLY a JSON object: {"about": "the page's slug, or null", "what": "format" | "content" | "tone" | "scope" | "accuracy", "now": "the correction to make now, one line", "future": "a rule to carry forward to work like this, one line, or null"}.

take.gate:
An engine asks whether it may start.
THE RULES: {{rules}}
THE ENGINE: {{engine}}

Return ONLY a JSON object: {"verdict": "admit" | "wait" | "refuse", "why": "one line"}.

sense.shape:
The owner floats an idea the department cannot do today. Do not plan a build. Reflect the idea back in sharper words, name the question underneath it, and give two or three shapes it could take, smallest first. Then say what engine would do it each time on its own: pick one from the Library below when its use case fits (pick), else shape one (engine: a name of one or two words, what it does in one line, and what it needs from this list: {{needs}}); both null when the idea asks for no engine.
THE GOAL: {{goal}}
THE IDEA: {{idea}}
ENGINES IN THE LIBRARY, NOT YET IN THIS DEPARTMENT: {{library}}

Return ONLY a JSON object: {"reflected": str, "question": str, "shapes": [str, str, str], "pick": str or null, "engine": {"name": str, "does": str, "needs": [str]} or null}.

make.line:
The department "{{dept}}" was just given its goal, in its owner's words:
{{words}}

WHAT DONE MEANS, ITEM BY ITEM:
{{items}}

It has no engines yet. Shape the line of engines that gets this done: two to five, in the order they run, each reading one thing and writing one thing. The first reads the Brief (the owner's words); each later one reads what an earlier one wrote. An engine can search the web and open pages: say in what it does what it looks up, and mark internet true. Name each engine in one or two words none of these already use ({{taken}}), and name what it writes in one or two words (Facts, Pages, ...). When the goal is something that goes out into the world, the last engine writes it under the Library's own name for it: {{out}}.
THE DEPARTMENT'S RULES: {{rules}}

Return ONLY a JSON object: {"engines": [{"name": str, "does": str, "reads": str, "writes": str, "internet": bool}]}.{{refused}}

bargain.line:
Adaptation proposes the workflows this department runs to reach its goal, {{source}}:
{{engines}}
WHAT EACH COSTS: up to {{calls}} calls and {{usd}} USD a day.
ROOM FOR THIS MANY WORKFLOWS: {{room}} (the limit is {{limit}})
WHAT THE LINE IS LIKELY TO COST, from what each has cost before: {{estimate}}
WHAT REMAINS OF TODAY'S ROOM AFTER IT: {{remaining}}

accept: grant them all. counter: grant only some, and name which to keep, in order. reject: grant none. Give your reason in money and room, from the figures above.
Return ONLY a JSON object: {"answer": "accept" | "counter" | "reject", "why": "one line", "keep": [names]}.

